  Now severity & "bites this run" assessment for each finding. Let me compile the final answer.

  Key findings list:

  1. (Q5/Q3) Non-Abort exceptions inside a cell (zlib.error, ValueError from array.frombytes/float/int in mzml_scan, binascii.Error) bypass the per-cell `except Abort` in run_group and CRASH the whole group: the second cell never runs, contradicting the documented "a failed cell does not stop the next one", and the entire ~26 h group re-runs. Same in add_split (only Abort caught) → crashes phase-2 worker mid-queue. Severity: should-fix (blocker-ish for robustness, but produces refusal not wrong numbers; realistic over 26h? only on malformed output).

  2. (Q7) share/OpenMS (OPENMS_DATA_PATH, 258 files read at runtime) is not hashed anywhere: not in cells_identity, not verified against PROVENANCE's share_OpenMS_tree_sha256 (cell_provenance only checks sha256_published entries for bin/FileFilter/lib), not in build_identity. env.sh itself not hashed either; an env.sh change pointing OPENMS_DATA_PATH elsewhere is invisible to G-V04/G-V11/G-V13. Should-fix; theoretical for this run unless someone touches the arm between launches (two launches at least: initial + any resume).

  3. (Q12/Q10) TMPDIR=jnatmp mode 0755: cell_env sets TMPDIR=q["jnatmp"]; G-V15 checks writability but not privacy. Patient-derived temp files (if diaWeaver/FileFilter write any) land world-readable, violating the patient-data rule that everything else enforces. Should-fix; bites this run if the tools use TMPDIR.

  4. (Q1) Plain-plan behavior change: plan with `entrapment: false` now accepted (was G-V01 unknown key). Nit. Also harmless.

  5. (Q9) Crash window between run_search writing ok record and add_split: record ok without by_charge/cells hash. Resume re-runs the search (search_done false) — fine; but render_cells_table's complete-group summary can KeyError on ["by_charge"] if ALL ok search records lack it (table_guards' one() passes with a single distinct measure). Should-fix/nit; bites if table rendered mid-run after an interrupted phase 2.

  6. (Q2) mzml_scan first-occurrence of PREC_CV: MS:1002815 at scan level vs selectedIon — first wins; if diaWeaver writes both with different values, digest/im stats use scan-level. Also self-closing `<spectrum/>` would silently break counting (theoretical; OpenMS always writes children). Also prec valueless cvParam → "" treated as missing — consistent before/after. Nit/should-fix depending on real output; verified facts say diaWeaver writes MS:1002815 per spectrum — location matters; the fake puts it in selectedIon. If the real file also has scan-level MS:1002815 (OpenMS's TDF loader often writes 1/K0 at scan level!), then... it's still consistent before/after for G-V17, and im_zero stats just reflect scan-level. Not a blocker.

  Wait, actually for diaWeaver output: mzml_scan(raw) — im_zero stat counts "1/K0 = 0 on the default .d path" — shown in cell table. If it reads scan-level instead of selectedIon-level... consistent. Fine.

  7. (Q3) G-V17 does not compare peak data before/after (before scanned with decode=False → no content_digest): FileFilter reordering a float array independently of m/z, or corrupting intensities, passes. Spectrum without m/z array passes G-V17 (fails later at Sage). Truncated array caught via length_mismatch; mislabelled compression caught via undecoded or crash (finding 1). Should-fix (documented gap) / theoretical since FileFilter is the pinned, trusted tool.

  8. (Q4) run_capped: kill semantics sound (session SIGKILL, BaseException cleanup). Residuals: (a) runner SIGKILL leaves orphan diaWeaver + staged copy; next launch's busy gate only WAITS 20 min then proceeds contended — orphan contention is measured/flagged, not aborted. (b) Memory-floor kill can be triggered by OTHER tenants on the shared 224-core node → kills a healthy 11-h cell → whole group re-runs (fail-safe, but a real availability risk for this run). (c) Race: tool finishes exactly as cap fires → recorded as killed despite success (fail-safe). Assessment: (b) worth noting; all fail-closed.

  9. (Q6) No-op digest: two runs of same arm → equal digest requires diaWeaver determinism; with 100 threads, if peak/trace assignment is thread-order dependent, dwv_default and dwv_pickim differ by noise → a REAL no-op is never flagged (the check can only false-negative, not false-positive). Conversely collision across different arms is impossible modulo sha256. So: G-V18 flags only if outputs are byte-content-equal; nondeterminism masks no-ops. Should be stated in the report (it partially is). Nit.

  Also ids_re conditional `if b"spectrumRef" in line` — id= on non-spectrumRef lines would leak into digest; in OpenMS output ids appear only on the spectrum open line and precursor spectrumRef... fine, nit.

  10. (Q8) sage_by_charge target_peptides can differ from sage_peptides target_peptides when a peptide has both target and decoy qualifying rows and the decoy row has the higher discriminant → G-V19 aborts (fail-closed, equality checked) — so inconsistency exists but is caught. Ties in best-score pick first row → deterministic. msf_by_charge ordering replicates msf_peptides tuple sort including decoy-first tie-break — consistent. entrap_strata partition enforced. So Q8: consistent, with the one caught exception.

  11. (Q11) render_cells_table: `s_z2 / d_sz2 if d_sz2 else float("nan")` → prints "nan" — cosmetic. KeyError risk as in finding 5. `arm()` returns "FAILED None" for missing arm — cosmetic. Numbers all from guarded records. Also summary `break` when not full — fine.

  Also check: `render_cells_table` per-row ratio `S["dt", g][0]["peptides"]` — dt peptides >0 guaranteed. OK.

  12. (Q10) stage_tdf: 0700 everywhere, two files only, deletion in finally incl. SIGTERM (BaseException), G-V14 escalation. Missed: nothing significant; note raw-side: nothing written beside raw (fingerprint reads ro). One nit: `shutil.copyfile` doesn't preserve... irrelevant. And umask — files created 0644&~umask inside 0700 dir — fine.

  One more check on run_group: `rec["gate"] = load_gate(q, patterns)` — gate BEFORE ref arms only; cells run hours later without re-gating? In run_pair the gate is once per pair; group same. By design (contention monitored during arms).

